.TH "kome" "1" "2026-10-21"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
kome - change the whole look of KDE Plasma 6 in one command
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBkome\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpreset\fR]
.PP
\fBkome\fR \fB-h\fR | \fB--help\fR | \fB--version\fR | \fB--commands\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBkome\fR themes the whole desktop from one palette: the Plasma colour scheme,
icons (with folders in the look'\&s accent colour), cursor, fonts, font
rendering, wallpaper and terminals (kitty, Ghostty).\& GTK apps follow through
Plasma'\&s own GTK sync.\&
.PP
It never needs root and never installs packages: it says what to install.\&
It writes only its own files, and adds at most one include line to a user'\&s
file, and only when asked (\fBkome doctor --fix\fR).\& Before every change it saves
the desktop, so \fBkome restore original\fR always brings back the desktop as it
was before kome, and \fBkome purge\fR removes every trace of kome.\&
.PP
Every warning or error ends with a \fBhint:\fR line giving the next command to
run.\&
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
Where a command takes a \fIpreset\fR, it defaults to \fBPreset=\fR in \fBkome.\&conf\fR(5),
else the active one.\&
.PP
\fBapply\fR [\fB-n\fR] [\fB-v\fR] [\fB--partial\fR] [\fIpreset\fR]
.RS 4
Apply a look.\& Checks every unit first: if something the preset needs is
missing, nothing is changed (see \fBdeps\fR).\& Then saves the desktop and
applies each unit in order.\& Applying the same look twice changes nothing.\&
.PP
\fB-n\fR, \fB--dry-run\fR: show what would be applied, change nothing.\&
.br
\fB-v\fR, \fB--verbose\fR: say what each unit does.\&
.br
\fB--partial\fR: apply what is possible even if something is missing.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBlist\fR
.RS 4
List the presets: their name, a tab, and their full name.\& Your own presets
override shipped ones with the same name.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstatus\fR [\fB-v\fR]
.RS 4
Show the active preset and, for each unit, whether it is still as kome
left it, was changed by hand since, or was skipped.\& \fB-v\fR shows what changed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdoctor\fR [\fB--info\fR] [\fB--fix\fR] [\fIpreset\fR]
.RS 4
Check what each unit can do here and why not: ok, missing (something to
install), optional, off (opt-in), absent (app not installed, with the
command to install it) or error.\& Also detects Plasma settings that would
undo the look (accent colour from the wallpaper).\&
.PP
\fB--info\fR: also print facts about this system (Plasma and KWin versions,
session, GPUs, font rendering, screens).\&
.br
\fB--fix\fR: apply the fixes found.\& Reversible ones (such as the one include
line kitty and Ghostty need) are applied directly; anything that changes a
Plasma setting asks first.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdeps\fR [\fIpreset\fR]
.RS 4
Print the command that installs what the preset is missing, for your
package manager (dnf, zypper, pacman, apt).\& kome never runs it.\& Optional
extras come after a \fB# optional\fR line.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBrestore\fR \fBoriginal\fR | \fBprevious\fR
.RS 4
\fBoriginal\fR: the desktop as it was before kome ever changed it.\&
.br
\fBprevious\fR: the desktop before the last \fBapply\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpurge\fR [\fB-y\fR]
.RS 4
Restore \fBoriginal\fR, then delete everything kome created (colour schemes,
icon themes, terminal themes, the lines it added to your files) and its
snapshots and state.\& Your own files in \fI~/.\&config/kome/\fR are kept.\& Asks
for confirmation; \fB-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR skips it (required without a terminal).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH UNITS
.PP
Each part of the look is a \fBunit\fR, run in this order:
.PP
